sometimes we have to wonder and  speculate about how someone comes to  hold radical beliefs or becomes  motivated to commit violence in the real  world and sometimes the people who do  those things will actually tell us and  we've actually figured that out with the  mag a bomber the mag a bomber is this 57  year old Florida man who sent all those  pipe bombs through the mail to Democrats  and was ultimately caught you'll  remember maybe images of his van covered  in right-wing messaging and stickers and  he has told us that he was radicalized  by Fox News along with other right-wing  media he pled guilty to 65 counts back  in March and there's a whole bunch of  court documents that have now been  released that are extremely insightful  as well as disturbing to be quite honest  with you and his attorney actually says  his attorney is safe through these court  documents that the magg a bomber quote  found light in Donald Trump that he  watched Fox News quote religiously and  specifically he was watching Fox &amp;  Friends in the morning and Hannity in  the evening check out this quote from  the court documents his infatuation with  the president began as something  personal not political when he was most  down mr saye cruel ID on self-help books  on tape to keep going Donald Trump's  books on success and business were his  favorites mr. seoc was an ardent Trump  fan and when Trump announced he was  running for president mr. seoc  enthusiastically supported him he began  watching Fox News religiously at the gym  planning his morning workout to coincide  with Fox &amp; Friends and his evenings to  dovetail with Hannity he became obsessed  with quote attacks from those he  perceived as Trump's enemies and the  court documents go on to outline that he  was not only radicalized through  right-wing media and the Internet but he  used that same Internet to also learn to  build the pipe bombs that he ultimately  ended up sending to Hillary Clinton and  Barack Obama George Soros and a number  of other people whose names escape me  so the real important takeaway here is  that the media stuff is not a game once  you understand the concept of stochastic  terrorism which I've talked about enough  this week I'm not going to redefine it  but google it or check out some of my  stories from our  this week about it when you understand  the sort of fundamental vulnerability of  so many people you really should have a  sense of responsibility for everything  that you say in a public forum in media  on TV or in a YouTube channel and the  radicalizing impact of extremist media  is just massive and if you what listen  to live calls on our show we've received  a lot of calls from people who call in  and say they were radicalized by you  know they will sometimes say it was Alex  Jones or Infowars stefan molyneux  Breitbart  could be Fox News could be the blaze  there are less well-known ones as well I  can't think of all of them offhand the  point is this is not an exception to the  rule the combination of extremely  outrageous content meant to foment anger  rather than activism that benefits the  majority of people or that improve  society this anger porn that is so  popular among particularly right-wing  media combined with the echo-chamber  algorithmic self-perpetuating loops that  people can get into on YouTube or in  other places online Twitter Facebook etc  this is meant to give people more and  more of what resonates with them the  most and what we have to understand is  that for many people that self that  constant feedback loop is going to leave  them to take real-world action this is  not me saying you know Facebook's  algorithm is a terroristic I'm not  saying that I'm not going that far I'm  not saying that when Glenn Beck rants  and raves about the tides foundation and  someone goes and tries to shoot up the  tides foundation that now Glenn Beck is  specifically guilty of a crime what I'm  saying is if we want to have an adult  conversation